WEBVTT

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:17.130
Nusumareta kako wo

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:20.330
Sagashitsuzukete

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.420
Ore wa samayou

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:27.130
Mishiranu machi wo

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:32.040
Honou no nioi shimitsuite

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:33.750
Museru

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:37.630
Sayonara wa itta hazu da

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.540
Wakareta hazu sa

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.790
Jigoku wo mireba

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.330
Kokoro ga kawaku

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:52.750
Tatakai wa akita no sa

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.540
Sadame to areba

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:00.790
Kokoro wo kimeru

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:05.960
Sottoshite oite kure

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.750
Ashita ni

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:15.250
Aa tsunagaru kyou gurai

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:43.920
It seemed that Killy, Rochina, and I
were three of a kind.

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:50.040
The ship we were on, under Wiseman's control,
travelled on through the darkness of space.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:53.000
Its destination still unknown to us.

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:08.540
Successor

00:02:09.170 --> 00:02:11.580
An object of enormous mass
is approaching dead ahead.

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:14.290
K-405, G-25. It's not putting out any light at all.

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:15.920
We're on a direct collision course!

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:17.790
Are you steering us?

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:20.290
No, sir. The ship isn't under our control.

00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:22.250
Then we'll have to just go along with it.

00:02:22.630 --> 00:02:23.540
But, sir...

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:25.040
And pray to God.

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:55.880
I don't believe it!

00:02:56.290 --> 00:02:59.080
Even class-A cosmologists
haven't conceived of these.

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:01.790
The existence of the technology of God!

00:03:05.630 --> 00:03:09.330
I'm afraid. I feel like something's
awakened inside you.

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:13.170
For some reason, I feel like you're going far away.

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:14.960
That we'll be separated.

00:03:15.580 --> 00:03:17.290
I don't understand you anymore.

00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:18.790
We'll understand, soon.

00:03:19.710 --> 00:03:21.880
And I want to know what this is, also.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:09.630
Are we dead yet?

00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:11.330
No, we're still alive.

00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:12.500
Thank goodness...

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:14.960
How long do you plan on holding me, then?

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:18.710
Don't kid me!

00:04:18.710 --> 00:04:19.540
I'm not!

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:35.210
It's all man-made...

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:36.080
Yeah...

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:16.130
Holy...

00:05:16.130 --> 00:05:17.210
No way...

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:18.080
What is it?

00:05:31.460 --> 00:05:34.250
A telepathic communications system
based on sound waves.

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:38.790
Yes. Some sort of pulse
that only certain people can sense.

00:05:38.790 --> 00:05:41.790
Must be sent directly through
their central nervous system.

00:05:41.790 --> 00:05:45.000
Isn't it highly improbable for
those three to be sensitive to it?

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:48.130
Our controller seems to be called "Wiseman."

00:05:48.330 --> 00:05:54.130
Perhaps these three share pasts
which brought them in contact with him?

00:05:54.380 --> 00:05:56.500
I don't see how that's possible.

00:05:56.500 --> 00:06:01.170
I can't see the three of them
sharing anything in common.

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:06.170
The theory's logical,
but I don't see how Chirico fits in.

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:08.920
Our only interest in this was developing the PS.

00:06:08.920 --> 00:06:10.420
That's over now.

00:06:10.830 --> 00:06:14.130
But I believe this is an opportunity
to switch specialties.

00:06:14.460 --> 00:06:15.960
I agree.

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:20.000
As you wish...

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:21.630
What was that? Chirico?

00:06:21.630 --> 00:06:22.500
Chirico?

00:06:23.130 --> 00:06:26.790
Wiseman wishes Chirico to be brought to him.

00:06:27.130 --> 00:06:28.790
I'm sure he said Chirico.

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:33.630
I thought all three of us had been
equally ordered by Wiseman.

00:06:33.630 --> 00:06:35.670
What's special about Chirico?

00:06:35.670 --> 00:06:39.460
He didn't say we couldn't go, sir.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:43.920
Rochina, Chirico seems to be important to him.

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:46.170
You're free to think what you like, sir.

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:47.750
But you know as much as I do.

00:06:47.750 --> 00:06:49.750
Don't play dumb with me!

00:06:49.750 --> 00:06:53.000
I'm sure you got some sort of data from Chirico!

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:54.080
Perhaps...

00:06:55.830 --> 00:06:58.670
What are you doing?
I brought Chirico to Wiseman!

00:06:58.670 --> 00:07:00.880
Your job is finished!

00:07:00.880 --> 00:07:03.290
I'll lead Chirico to him!

00:07:05.880 --> 00:07:09.000
Lock Rochina up with Proto One.

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:09.880
Yes, sir!

00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:13.580
Chirico!

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:17.710
Don't worry, Fyana.

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:20.880
If anything happens to her, you'll be sorry!

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:21.920
You betcha!

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:24.080
Oh, you people.

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:25.540
Take them as well!

00:07:25.540 --> 00:07:27.210
Huh? What're you doing?

00:07:27.210 --> 00:07:28.210
Lemme go, you creep!

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:29.500
Chirico, be careful!

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:50.960
Wherever we are,
it's definitely the end of the line.

00:07:50.960 --> 00:07:55.040
This ship isn't Gilgamesh or Balarant.
Meaning what?

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:58.250
Whatever it means,
I don't like the looks of these guys!

00:07:58.250 --> 00:08:01.500
Hey! Let us out! Come on!

00:08:03.710 --> 00:08:04.830
Jerks!

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:10.080
We're not gonna leave this ship.

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:11.540
Why's that, Pops?

00:08:12.170 --> 00:08:13.330
Chirico.

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:15.130
What about him?

00:08:15.880 --> 00:08:17.330
Haven't you noticed?

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:20.000
Rochina and the others
were looking for the PS.

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:21.250
You mean Fyana?

00:08:21.250 --> 00:08:26.670
Right. And for that they've been
sticking to Chirico's ass like a piece of shit.

00:08:26.960 --> 00:08:29.130
Yeah, now that you mention it, that's right.

00:08:31.290 --> 00:08:32.960
I have the worst luck!

00:08:36.920 --> 00:08:38.500
I don't like the looks of this.

00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:39.210
No kidding.

00:08:39.210 --> 00:08:40.000
Pops!

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:40.670
Right!

00:08:40.670 --> 00:08:41.920
Get in there!

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:44.630
What'll we do?

00:08:44.630 --> 00:08:45.880
Lemme handle this.

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:48.420
Hey, before you kill us, can I ask one thing?

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:50.290
What's happened to our friend?

00:08:50.580 --> 00:08:52.750
Rochina dies after we kill you.

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:56.170
No, I mean Chirico! The young guy.

00:08:56.170 --> 00:08:58.710
Going ashore. Aside from that: No comment!

00:08:58.710 --> 00:09:01.710
Uh, hold on! Can I ask one more thing?

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:04.040
You're a pain in the ass, you know that? What?

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:07.500
Can I just have one last cigarette? Please?

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:11.170
You're a real bastard if you won't
give him that much.

00:09:12.290 --> 00:09:14.920
I would've given him one
without the smart comment. Come here!

00:09:16.290 --> 00:09:17.630
Okay...

00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:20.880
Thanks pal. Thanks a bunch.

00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:22.290
Uh, got a light?

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:23.290
Here!

00:09:31.290 --> 00:09:33.420
Been too long since I've had one of these...

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:34.170
What's wrong?

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:35.290
This!

00:09:36.960 --> 00:09:37.920
Why, you...!

00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:38.630
Freeze!

00:09:39.040 --> 00:09:40.250
Sorry, fellas!

00:09:40.250 --> 00:09:41.500
Heave...

00:09:41.500 --> 00:09:42.670
...Ho!

00:09:46.670 --> 00:09:47.830
Okay!

00:09:47.830 --> 00:09:48.540
We did it!

00:09:48.540 --> 00:09:49.710
It actually worked!

00:09:49.710 --> 00:09:51.710
Pops, grab a gun and let's get out of here!

00:09:51.710 --> 00:09:53.540
Right, gotcha!

00:09:54.040 --> 00:09:58.080
You really think you idiots can get off this ship?

00:09:58.080 --> 00:09:59.580
You're the idiot, pal.

00:10:00.580 --> 00:10:03.000
Vanilla, hurry up!

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:05.000
Right! Coming!

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:10.460
What's going to happen to Chirico?

00:10:10.460 --> 00:10:12.460
I'd like to know that myself.

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:13.460
No talking!

00:10:13.830 --> 00:10:15.960
No talking from you, either!

00:10:15.960 --> 00:10:17.630
I said shut up!

00:10:18.710 --> 00:10:20.420
They're here. Enter!

00:10:24.080 --> 00:10:25.670
Captain, what's wrong?

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:27.080
Ta-daa!

00:10:27.710 --> 00:10:28.710
Captain!

00:10:28.710 --> 00:10:29.750
Drop your guns!

00:10:29.750 --> 00:10:33.040
Or who knows what'll happen
to the poor Captain here.

00:10:33.040 --> 00:10:34.580
Drop them, now!

00:10:36.380 --> 00:10:38.750
Okay, now move over there.

00:10:41.080 --> 00:10:42.750
Fyana! Come on!

00:10:45.460 --> 00:10:46.750
Whoops!

00:10:46.750 --> 00:10:48.500
What do we do with this gentleman?

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:50.330
He's been SO nice to us, after all.

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:52.630
We can pay him back really well, now.

00:10:52.630 --> 00:10:54.630
I know where Chirico's going.

00:10:56.130 --> 00:10:58.580
We've been on ice for a while now.

00:10:58.580 --> 00:11:00.330
I want some news, pal.

00:11:01.210 --> 00:11:02.750
All right. I'll tell you.

00:11:02.750 --> 00:11:03.750
Okay!

00:11:04.710 --> 00:11:06.130
Let's go, Pops!

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:12.040
You're a dangerous man.

00:11:12.040 --> 00:11:14.290
Pardon our not giving you a gun.

00:11:50.040 --> 00:11:52.420
It destroyed our ships and theirs in an instant?

00:11:52.420 --> 00:11:53.500
Impossible!

00:11:53.500 --> 00:11:54.880
Yet it happened!

00:11:54.880 --> 00:11:56.880
We have to issue a protest to Quent!

00:11:56.880 --> 00:11:59.830
Like they have a formal government to protest to?

00:11:59.830 --> 00:12:01.830
Then how do we negotiate?

00:12:01.830 --> 00:12:03.210
We can't talk to them!

00:12:03.210 --> 00:12:07.330
Quent's the biggest taboo in the Astragius Galaxy.

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:09.750
True, we have very little data on Quent.

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:14.210
However, projects by our historians and
scientists are working to solve that problem.

00:12:14.380 --> 00:12:17.710
It's just a question of time
until we have all the facts.

00:12:17.710 --> 00:12:18.880
Do we have any options open?

00:12:18.880 --> 00:12:22.710
Yes. There are survivors of our forces
stationed on Quent.

00:12:23.170 --> 00:12:28.170
According to their reports, the only things
which were destroyed were the battleships.

00:12:28.170 --> 00:12:29.670
Which nation is responsible?

00:12:29.670 --> 00:12:31.380
A third power, apparently.

00:12:31.920 --> 00:12:34.670
Our scout patrols are still investigating that.

00:12:34.670 --> 00:12:36.130
A third power?

00:12:36.130 --> 00:12:37.080
General!

00:12:37.880 --> 00:12:39.290
I have a suggestion.

00:12:39.290 --> 00:12:40.080
Let's hear it.

00:12:40.080 --> 00:12:44.420
Since both the Gilgamesh and the Balarant
were the victims in this battle,

00:12:44.420 --> 00:12:48.920
we won't solve anything by treating it
as a simple border skirmish.

00:12:49.290 --> 00:12:53.500
I say again that we should call a meeting of
the Galactic Assembly with the Balarant!

00:12:53.500 --> 00:12:54.380
He's right!

00:12:54.380 --> 00:12:55.380
It's the only way!

00:12:55.380 --> 00:12:56.420
Quiet!

00:12:56.880 --> 00:12:59.130
I agree with all of you.

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:02.330
Let's try to get the Assembly called
as quickly as possible.

00:13:13.540 --> 00:13:15.130
This is quite a deep passageway.

00:13:15.130 --> 00:13:16.710
And it looks like there're even more here.

00:13:41.540 --> 00:13:43.040
Soon now.

00:13:43.040 --> 00:13:45.460
The entrance to Wiseman's shrine.

00:13:57.630 --> 00:13:59.170
What the...?

00:14:04.790 --> 00:14:06.000
A dead end?

00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:07.710
No, there's something here.

00:14:07.710 --> 00:14:10.750
How rude! Even with an invitation,
we can't go all the way.

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:14.500
Those who Wiseman does not want cannot come.

00:14:55.920 --> 00:14:57.670
Is this our destination?

00:14:58.500 --> 00:14:59.630
Look!

00:15:03.670 --> 00:15:05.670
At last, I can see him face-to-face!

00:15:07.170 --> 00:15:10.540
Now we begin our research
into what makes Chirico special.

00:15:10.540 --> 00:15:13.500
Considering that every possibility is hidden,

00:15:13.500 --> 00:15:15.500
finding it will be wonderfully difficult!

00:15:17.040 --> 00:15:19.290
My dream has come true.

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:22.170
The will of Wiseman is absolute!

00:15:22.170 --> 00:15:26.710
With even a piece of his power,
I can rule the entire galaxy!

00:15:34.670 --> 00:15:37.080
God dammit, I'll make them pay for this!

00:15:37.080 --> 00:15:39.330
If you find them, shoot on sight!

00:15:45.750 --> 00:15:48.290
So, in other words, you got the jump on them.

00:15:48.290 --> 00:15:50.670
I can't tell you anymore.

00:15:50.670 --> 00:15:52.630
Only that Chirico is necessary for me.

00:15:52.630 --> 00:15:54.080
Well, whatever.

00:15:54.080 --> 00:15:56.920
We've all got the same objectives.

00:15:56.920 --> 00:15:59.130
Yeah, we owe this to Chirico.

00:15:59.130 --> 00:16:00.540
This time, we'll save him.

00:16:00.710 --> 00:16:04.750
I just don't see why everyone's
all bug-eyed over Chirico now.

00:16:04.750 --> 00:16:06.630
Chirico isn't a human like you.

00:16:06.630 --> 00:16:09.130
He's an existence beyond even that of the PS.

00:16:09.420 --> 00:16:13.460
I don't understand the complicated parts,
but Chirico's our friend. And he's human.

00:16:13.460 --> 00:16:16.250
Exactly! Stop making him sound like a monster!

00:16:16.250 --> 00:16:17.920
I feel sorry for him!

00:16:18.250 --> 00:16:19.790
You feel sorry for him?

00:16:19.790 --> 00:16:21.170
Considering that Chirico's-

00:16:21.170 --> 00:16:22.670
Oh, why even bother telling you?

00:16:22.670 --> 00:16:24.330
Is Chirico...?

00:16:25.080 --> 00:16:28.460
He's fine. Don't worry. Chirico's immortal.

00:16:28.460 --> 00:16:30.210
Immortal? Exactly.

00:16:30.210 --> 00:16:32.580
Chirico receives his life from Wiseman himself-

00:16:39.040 --> 00:16:42.130
Hey, aren't those the guards from before?

00:16:42.130 --> 00:16:43.460
Looks like them.

00:16:43.460 --> 00:16:45.630
We let them live and now this!

00:16:45.630 --> 00:16:47.290
Of all the ungrateful...!

00:16:47.290 --> 00:16:48.460
Bastards!

00:16:50.540 --> 00:16:53.210
Okay, we'll handle this. Get going!

00:16:53.830 --> 00:16:55.330
Pops, take over!

00:16:55.330 --> 00:16:56.330
Right!

00:16:56.920 --> 00:16:58.500
Huh? What?

00:16:58.500 --> 00:17:01.210
What am I supposed to do by myself?

00:17:03.170 --> 00:17:05.460
Vanilla! Wait for me!

00:17:25.790 --> 00:17:27.170
What's wrong?

00:17:27.170 --> 00:17:28.210
Soldiers.

00:17:28.210 --> 00:17:30.080
What? What'll we do?

00:17:30.080 --> 00:17:31.210
Leave this to me.

00:17:31.830 --> 00:17:34.960
You think His Excellency and the others
are with Wiseman now?

00:17:34.960 --> 00:17:37.040
Who knows? Hey! What are you doing here?

00:17:37.210 --> 00:17:38.790
Wait! Don't shoot!

00:17:39.380 --> 00:17:42.080
You're that Rochina guy, aren't you?

00:17:42.080 --> 00:17:43.500
I thought you were locked up!

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:44.750
You escaped, didn't you?

00:17:44.750 --> 00:17:47.880
No! Didn't you get the orders from Gen. Killy?

00:17:47.880 --> 00:17:48.710
What?

00:17:48.710 --> 00:17:51.460
Wiseman orders that I be let through!

00:17:51.460 --> 00:17:53.500
We didn't get any order like that!

00:17:53.500 --> 00:17:54.790
It's an emergency!

00:17:54.790 --> 00:17:55.630
Freeze!

00:17:55.630 --> 00:17:57.330
If you think I'm lying,
then you can keep me here!

00:17:57.330 --> 00:17:59.500
But be ready to face
the consequences for doing it!

00:17:59.500 --> 00:18:01.670
His Excellency is in a hurry!

00:18:02.500 --> 00:18:03.540
Way to go!

00:18:03.540 --> 00:18:05.080
Sorry I'm late!

00:18:06.170 --> 00:18:07.040
Vanilla!

00:18:08.540 --> 00:18:09.250
Idiots!

00:18:09.250 --> 00:18:11.630
You moron, it was working!

00:18:11.630 --> 00:18:13.040
Escapees!

00:18:13.210 --> 00:18:14.460
Uh-oh! Run!

00:18:15.210 --> 00:18:16.380
I knew it!

00:18:16.380 --> 00:18:17.460
I'm not with them!

00:18:17.460 --> 00:18:18.380
Shut up!

00:18:41.210 --> 00:18:42.710
Right ahead of us...

00:18:43.710 --> 00:18:45.040
We're here.

00:18:45.580 --> 00:18:47.920
You two will remain here.

00:18:47.920 --> 00:18:49.790
Come, Chirico. Let's go.

00:18:49.790 --> 00:18:50.920
Wiseman...

00:18:51.250 --> 00:18:54.420
Wiseman! I'm here with Chirico!

00:18:54.750 --> 00:18:56.880
What? Only Chirico?

00:18:57.420 --> 00:19:00.080
Why? Why only him?

00:19:00.080 --> 00:19:01.290
Wiseman!

00:19:01.290 --> 00:19:03.460
Obey the will of Wiseman.

00:19:09.630 --> 00:19:11.750
Wiseman! Let me come, too!

00:19:17.580 --> 00:19:19.170
Why can't I...?

00:19:19.170 --> 00:19:20.790
Why only Chirico...?

00:19:20.790 --> 00:19:21.580
No!

00:19:45.920 --> 00:19:48.880
Wiseman, what you say seems to be true.

00:19:49.330 --> 00:19:52.750
I don't mind that my destiny
has always been under your control.

00:19:52.750 --> 00:19:54.170
That's why I've come.

00:19:56.210 --> 00:19:57.380
But, why?

00:19:58.750 --> 00:20:00.330
What? I am?

00:20:02.250 --> 00:20:04.500
But how is that different from a PS?

00:20:06.670 --> 00:20:08.330
That's right.

00:20:08.330 --> 00:20:11.080
They were both artificially enhanced humans.

00:20:11.960 --> 00:20:13.750
That's what PSs are.

00:20:13.750 --> 00:20:15.500
But then, why could I...?

00:20:17.250 --> 00:20:19.080
I was born a PS?

00:20:19.080 --> 00:20:20.500
An... An "Overman?"

00:20:24.630 --> 00:20:26.290
I'm just like you?

00:20:28.290 --> 00:20:29.750
What do you mean?

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:40.080
I was born out of the history of Astragius?

00:20:40.630 --> 00:20:42.630
Your successor?

00:20:48.790 --> 00:20:49.830
Wait.

00:20:53.330 --> 00:20:55.670
I'm to rule the galaxy...

00:20:56.670 --> 00:20:58.210
In your place...

00:21:14.960 --> 00:21:16.290
Very well.

00:21:16.290 --> 00:21:18.790
I will gladly become your successor.

00:21:18.790 --> 00:21:19.960
Starting now.

00:21:58.790 --> 00:22:00.460
What? It's over?

00:22:00.460 --> 00:22:02.040
My role in this?

00:22:03.380 --> 00:22:05.250
That's all I was here for?

00:22:05.540 --> 00:22:06.880
Wiseman!

00:22:26.790 --> 00:22:27.880
Chirico...

00:22:37.080 --> 00:22:39.330
I was Wiseman's successor.

00:22:40.380 --> 00:22:42.540
His will had determined that for me.

00:22:43.790 --> 00:22:48.170
I could finally see my destiny
unfolding before me.

00:22:49.130 --> 00:22:51.460
Because I was one of the Children of God.

00:22:54.290 --> 00:22:55.710
Next Episode

00:22:56.290 --> 00:23:00.500
The joy and pain in man's world
is the merest twinkle of a star.

00:23:00.960 --> 00:23:02.250
The eternal movements of creation.

00:23:02.250 --> 00:23:06.210
All is arranged within the cosmos,
but only visible via a great illumination.

00:23:07.000 --> 00:23:09.420
In the bottomless reaches of space,
on a lonely throne,

00:23:09.420 --> 00:23:15.670
sits one who has overseen the changes
in uncounted stars for ages beyond knowing.

00:23:16.130 --> 00:23:17.580
But who is he?

00:23:18.130 --> 00:23:19.750
Next time, "Overman"

00:23:19.750 --> 00:23:24.290
Overman

00:23:19.750 --> 00:23:24.290
Next Time

00:23:20.540 --> 00:23:22.290
It may well be our destiny.

00:23:42.540 --> 00:23:46.000
Samishii toki mo

00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:49.540
Kanashii toki mo

00:23:49.540 --> 00:23:55.920
Itsumo anata ga me ni ukabu

00:23:56.420 --> 00:23:59.960
Hitori no toki mo

00:23:59.960 --> 00:24:03.380
Aitai toki mo

00:24:03.380 --> 00:24:09.630
Itsumo anata wa mune no naka

00:24:09.630 --> 00:24:13.130
Tooku hanarete itemo

00:24:13.130 --> 00:24:16.540
Tatoe wakarete itemo

00:24:16.710 --> 00:24:23.040
Kono yo no hikari to tomo ni mabushiku

00:24:23.420 --> 00:24:29.380
Ano hi no anata ga...
